Description: terminal multiplexer (latest upstream release)
 tmux enables a number of terminals (or windows) to be accessed and
 controlled from a single terminal like screen. tmux runs as a
 server-client system. A server is created automatically when necessary
 and holds a number of sessions, each of which may have a number of
 windows linked to it. Any number of clients may connect to a session,
 or the server may be controlled by issuing commands with tmux.
 .
 This package tracks every tagged tmux release. It is compiled from
 upstream's release tarball with systemd, jemalloc and sixel support, and
 with ncurses' terminfo library linked statically so every terminal
 feature works on old and new suites alike. It replaces the
 distribution's tmux in place. Sessions already running keep the old
 server until they exit or `tmux kill-server` is run.
